# Trivy ignore list for the Alauda trivy fork.
#
# Each entry must include: CVE id, why it is ignored, and a re-check trigger.
# Remove entries once the underlying package can be upgraded to a clean version.

# CVE-2026-34040 (HIGH) - Moby AuthZ plugin bypass with oversized request body.
# CVE-2026-33997 (MEDIUM) - Related Moby CVE flagged on the same pseudo-version.
#
# Both advisories declare the fixed version as Docker Engine 29.3.1, which only
# exists on the new `github.com/moby/moby/v2` module path. This branch already
# uses `github.com/docker/docker` at `github.com/moby/moby` 28.x HEAD
# (`v28.5.3-0.20260325154711-31a1689cb0a1+incompatible`), which already contains
# the upstream AuthZ backport commits (`pkg/authz: Reject requests exceeding
# body size limit`, `pkg/authz: Increase body limit to 4 MiB`,
# `plugin: Fix off-by-one in privilege validation`). The scanner cannot tell
# from the pseudo-version string that the fix is included, so it keeps the
# advisories open.
#
# Re-check trigger: drop these entries once a tagged `v28.5.3+` release lands
# on `github.com/moby/moby` 28.x, or once this fork migrates to the
# `github.com/moby/moby/v2` module path with a >=29.3.1 release.
CVE-2026-34040
CVE-2026-33997

# CVE-2026-50163 (HIGH) - oras-go tar extraction: hardlink entry with relative
# Linkname can escape the extract dir via process CWD resolution
# (content/file/utils.go ensureLinkPath).
#
# No fixed version is published upstream as of 2026-07-06: the advisory lists
# oras.land/oras-go/v2 as "affected" with FixedVersion empty, and v2.6.1 (the
# latest release, already in use here) does not carry the fix. There is no
# clean version to upgrade to.
#
# Re-check trigger: drop this entry once oras-project/oras-go ships a release
# that lists a FixedVersion for CVE-2026-50163.
CVE-2026-50163
